Here is the root cause:
The bug was caused by the absence of the `RETAIN_FF_ENABLE` flag in the GDSC structures for the SM8550, which prevented the GDSCs from retaining their state when entering lower power modes. This could lead to loss of functionality or improper operation of the components managed by these GDSCs after transitioning to and from low power states.

